### Rationale
The 256-bit accesses were the S-band problem, so H12 is supported. The 128-bit layout with 16 lanes per row and 128-thread CTAs beat r0 at every size I scanned, with both kernels in their dispatched configuration. Each variant was timed interleaved with r0 for 5 repeats (3 at 2.7 GB). The full 16-workload run_tests gave 16/16 pass and S −9.4%, M −6.2%, L −6.3%. It also gave a predicted portal score of 0.665, against 0.635 for r0.

The success criteria are met at 2.2 MB (−0.3 us, the target was 0.25) and at 15.8 MB. At 6.6 MB the gain is only −1.7%, below the 3% target.

